    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling matchups against soft-tossing righties. **Corbin Carroll** (80.77) remains our premier start; despite a slight penalty for the platoon disadvantage against Abbott, the combination of a 5.01 xERA starter and his elite speed profile keeps him at the top of our board. Following closely, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) is a mandatory start against Waguespack. His dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and favorable order placement make him the anchor of our infield production today. **Gabriel Moreno** (66.77) and **Henry Bolte** (60.79) round out our top-tier plays, both benefiting significantly from the soft matchups against Abbott and Javier, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Isaac Paredes**, who posted a 45.78, narrowly missing the cut behind the marginally higher efficiency of **Jose Caballero** and **Mickey Moniak**. While **Isaac Paredes** has the pedigree, his struggles against the southpaw Basso necessitated a move to the bench in favor of hitters with more favorable platoon splits. We are also keeping a close watch on **Mickey Moniak**, whose score of 54.50 is bolstered by a +14% park factor, though his -15% platoon penalty against Griffin keeps him squarely in the \"marginal\" bucket. \n\nRisk management remains paramount, specifically regarding the heavy hitters facing elite arms. **Seiya Suzuki** (49.48) and **Josh Naylor** (49.18) are facing uphill battles against Miller and Imanaga; their scores are suppressed by the quality of the opposing staff, making them low-floor options today. We are also monitoring the status of **James Wood**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving a hole in our outfield depth that requires careful management of our remaining bench assets like **Griffin Conine** and **Cole Young**. With SB at a premium, the speed profiles of **Brice Turang** and **Henry Bolte** will be the deciding factors if our counting stats remain stagnant heading into the late-game window.",
